              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Overview\nArchive Slip is a path traversal vulnerability that occurs when extracting\narchive files (zip, tar, jar). An attacker crafts a malicious archive with\nentries like `../../etc/passwd` that, when extracted, write files outside\nthe intended directory.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.zip.*;\n\npublic class Extractor {\n    public void extract(String zipPath, String destDir) throws Exception {\n        ZipInputStream zis = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(zipPath));\n        ZipEntry entry;\n        while ((entry = zis.getNextEntry()) != null) {\n            // Vulnerable: entry.getName() may contain \"../\"\n            File outFile = new File(destDir, entry.getName());\n            FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(outFile);\n            byte[] buf = new byte[1024];\n            int len;\n            while ((len = zis.read(buf)) > 0) fos.write(buf, 0, len);\n            fos.close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Remediation\nValidate that the resolved path stays within the target directory.\n\n```java\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.zip.*;\n\npublic class Extractor {\n    public void extract(String zipPath, String destDir) throws Exception {\n        File dest = new File(destDir).getCanonicalFile();\n        ZipInputStream zis = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(zipPath));\n        ZipEntry entry;\n        while ((entry = zis.getNextEntry()) != null) {\n            File outFile = new File(dest, entry.getName()).getCanonicalFile();\n            if (!outFile.getPath().startsWith(dest.getPath())) {\n                throw new IOException(\"Archive entry outside target dir: \" + entry.getName());\n            }\n            FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(outFile);\n            byte[] buf = new byte[1024];\n            int len;\n            while ((len = zis.read(buf)) > 0) fos.write(buf, 0, len);\n            fos.close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n",
                "text": "### Overview\nArchive Slip is a path traversal vulnerability that occurs when extracting\narchive files (zip, tar, jar). An attacker crafts a malicious archive with\nentries like `../../etc/passwd` that, when extracted, write files outside\nthe intended directory.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.zip.*;\n\npublic class Extractor {\n    public void extract(String zipPath, String destDir) throws Exception {\n        ZipInputStream zis = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(zipPath));\n        ZipEntry entry;\n        while ((entry = zis.getNextEntry()) != null) {\n            // Vulnerable: entry.getName() may contain \"../\"\n            File outFile = new File(destDir, entry.getName());\n            FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(outFile);\n            byte[] buf = new byte[1024];\n            int len;\n            while ((len = zis.read(buf)) > 0) fos.write(buf, 0, len);\n            fos.close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Remediation\nValidate that the resolved path stays within the target directory.\n\n```java\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.zip.*;\n\npublic class Extractor {\n    public void extract(String zipPath, String destDir) throws Exception {\n        File dest = new File(destDir).getCanonicalFile();\n        ZipInputStream zis = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(zipPath));\n        ZipEntry entry;\n        while ((entry = zis.getNextEntry()) != null) {\n            File outFile = new File(dest, entry.getName()).getCanonicalFile();\n            if (!outFile.getPath().startsWith(dest.getPath())) {\n                throw new IOException(\"Archive entry outside target dir: \" + entry.getName());\n            }\n            FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(outFile);\n            byte[] buf = new byte[1024];\n            int len;\n            while ((len = zis.read(buf)) > 0) fos.write(buf, 0, len);\n            fos.close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "### Overview\nArchive Slip is a path traversal vulnerability that occurs when extracting\narchive files (zip, tar, jar). An attacker crafts a malicious archive with\nentries like `../../etc/passwd` that, when extracted, write files outside\nthe intended directory.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.zip.*;\n\npublic class Extractor {\n    public void extract(String zipPath, String destDir) throws Exception {\n        ZipInputStream zis = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(zipPath));\n        ZipEntry entry;\n        while ((entry = zis.getNextEntry()) != null) {\n            // Vulnerable: entry.getName() may contain \"../\"\n            File outFile = new File(destDir, entry.getName());\n            FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(outFile);\n            byte[] buf = new byte[1024];\n            int len;\n            while ((len = zis.read(buf)) > 0) fos.write(buf, 0, len);\n            fos.close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Remediation\nValidate that the resolved path stays within the target directory.\n\n```java\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.zip.*;\n\npublic class Extractor {\n    public void extract(String zipPath, String destDir) throws Exception {\n        File dest = new File(destDir).getCanonicalFile();\n        ZipInputStream zis = new ZipInputStream(new FileInputStream(zipPath));\n        ZipEntry entry;\n        while ((entry = zis.getNextEntry()) != null) {\n            File outFile = new File(dest, entry.getName()).getCanonicalFile();\n            if (!outFile.getPath().startsWith(dest.getPath())) {\n                throw new IOException(\"Archive entry outside target dir: \" + entry.getName());\n            }\n            FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(outFile);\n            byte[] buf = new byte[1024];\n            int len;\n            while ((len = zis.read(buf)) > 0) fos.write(buf, 0, len);\n            fos.close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n"
              },
