              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "### Overview\nPrivilege escalation involves exploiting a bug, design flaw, or configuration\noversight in an operating system or software application to gain elevated access\nto resources that are normally protected from an application or user. This\nallows an application or user to attain more privileges than intended by the\napplication developer or system administrator, enabling the performance of\nunauthorized actions.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\n\npublic class ElevatePrivileges {\n    public static void elevateFrogPrivileges(String username) throws IOException {\n        // Explicitly compare the username with administrative roles\n        if (\"admin\".equals(username)) {\n            // Execute improper elevation\n            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(\"sudo su\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        System.out.print(\"Enter frog username: \");\n        String user = reader.readLine();\n        elevateFrogPrivileges(user);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this example, the code attempts to elevate privileges for the specified\nuser. Anyone who can control the input `username` can potentially elevate\ntheir privileges by tricking the system.\n\n### Remediation\n```java\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\n\npublic class SafeElevatePrivileges {\n    // Check if the username is in the allowed list from environment variables\n    public static boolean isValidFrogUser(String username) {\n        String allowedUsers = System.getenv(\"ALLOWED_USERS\");\n        if (allowedUsers == null) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Environment variable ALLOWED_USERS is not set\");\n        }\n\n        String[] usersArray = allowedUsers.split(\",\");\n        for (String user : usersArray) {\n            if (user.equals(username)) {\n                return true;\n            }\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    // Function that safely attempts to elevate privileges for validated usernames\n    public static void elevateFrogPrivileges(String username) {\n        if (!isValidFrogUser(username)) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Unauthorized privilege escalation attempt by: \" + username);\n        }\n\n        // Construct and execute the sudo command with the validated username\n        String command = \"sudo -u \" + username + \" -s\";\n        try {\n            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);\n            System.out.println(\"Privileges elevated for user: \" + username);\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Failed to execute sudo command\", e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        try {\n            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n            System.out.print(\"Enter frog username: \");\n            String user = reader.readLine();\n            elevateFrogPrivileges(user);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            System.err.println(e.getMessage());\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\nTo remediate this vulnerability, check and validate that the `username`\nmatches an allowed user from an environment variable. This prevents\nunauthorized privilege escalation attempts by ensuring only authorized\nusers can elevate their privileges and securely indicates the elevation.",
                "text": "### Overview\nPrivilege escalation involves exploiting a bug, design flaw, or configuration\noversight in an operating system or software application to gain elevated access\nto resources that are normally protected from an application or user. This\nallows an application or user to attain more privileges than intended by the\napplication developer or system administrator, enabling the performance of\nunauthorized actions.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\n\npublic class ElevatePrivileges {\n    public static void elevateFrogPrivileges(String username) throws IOException {\n        // Explicitly compare the username with administrative roles\n        if (\"admin\".equals(username)) {\n            // Execute improper elevation\n            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(\"sudo su\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        System.out.print(\"Enter frog username: \");\n        String user = reader.readLine();\n        elevateFrogPrivileges(user);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this example, the code attempts to elevate privileges for the specified\nuser. Anyone who can control the input `username` can potentially elevate\ntheir privileges by tricking the system.\n\n### Remediation\n```java\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\n\npublic class SafeElevatePrivileges {\n    // Check if the username is in the allowed list from environment variables\n    public static boolean isValidFrogUser(String username) {\n        String allowedUsers = System.getenv(\"ALLOWED_USERS\");\n        if (allowedUsers == null) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Environment variable ALLOWED_USERS is not set\");\n        }\n\n        String[] usersArray = allowedUsers.split(\",\");\n        for (String user : usersArray) {\n            if (user.equals(username)) {\n                return true;\n            }\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    // Function that safely attempts to elevate privileges for validated usernames\n    public static void elevateFrogPrivileges(String username) {\n        if (!isValidFrogUser(username)) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Unauthorized privilege escalation attempt by: \" + username);\n        }\n\n        // Construct and execute the sudo command with the validated username\n        String command = \"sudo -u \" + username + \" -s\";\n        try {\n            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);\n            System.out.println(\"Privileges elevated for user: \" + username);\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Failed to execute sudo command\", e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        try {\n            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n            System.out.print(\"Enter frog username: \");\n            String user = reader.readLine();\n            elevateFrogPrivileges(user);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            System.err.println(e.getMessage());\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\nTo remediate this vulnerability, check and validate that the `username`\nmatches an allowed user from an environment variable. This prevents\nunauthorized privilege escalation attempts by ensuring only authorized\nusers can elevate their privileges and securely indicates the elevation."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "### Overview\nPrivilege escalation involves exploiting a bug, design flaw, or configuration\noversight in an operating system or software application to gain elevated access\nto resources that are normally protected from an application or user. This\nallows an application or user to attain more privileges than intended by the\napplication developer or system administrator, enabling the performance of\nunauthorized actions.\n\n### Vulnerable example\n```java\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\n\npublic class ElevatePrivileges {\n    public static void elevateFrogPrivileges(String username) throws IOException {\n        // Explicitly compare the username with administrative roles\n        if (\"admin\".equals(username)) {\n            // Execute improper elevation\n            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(\"sudo su\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        System.out.print(\"Enter frog username: \");\n        String user = reader.readLine();\n        elevateFrogPrivileges(user);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this example, the code attempts to elevate privileges for the specified\nuser. Anyone who can control the input `username` can potentially elevate\ntheir privileges by tricking the system.\n\n### Remediation\n```java\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.io.IOException;\n\npublic class SafeElevatePrivileges {\n    // Check if the username is in the allowed list from environment variables\n    public static boolean isValidFrogUser(String username) {\n        String allowedUsers = System.getenv(\"ALLOWED_USERS\");\n        if (allowedUsers == null) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Environment variable ALLOWED_USERS is not set\");\n        }\n\n        String[] usersArray = allowedUsers.split(\",\");\n        for (String user : usersArray) {\n            if (user.equals(username)) {\n                return true;\n            }\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    // Function that safely attempts to elevate privileges for validated usernames\n    public static void elevateFrogPrivileges(String username) {\n        if (!isValidFrogUser(username)) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Unauthorized privilege escalation attempt by: \" + username);\n        }\n\n        // Construct and execute the sudo command with the validated username\n        String command = \"sudo -u \" + username + \" -s\";\n        try {\n            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);\n            System.out.println(\"Privileges elevated for user: \" + username);\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\"Failed to execute sudo command\", e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        try {\n            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n            System.out.print(\"Enter frog username: \");\n            String user = reader.readLine();\n            elevateFrogPrivileges(user);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            System.err.println(e.getMessage());\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\nTo remediate this vulnerability, check and validate that the `username`\nmatches an allowed user from an environment variable. This prevents\nunauthorized privilege escalation attempts by ensuring only authorized\nusers can elevate their privileges and securely indicates the elevation."
