                "markdown": "### Overview\nInadequate RSA Padding occurs when RSA encryption is used with a padding \nscheme that provides insufficient security. This can lead to vulnerabilities \nsuch as plaintext recovery, chosen-ciphertext attacks, and other cryptographic \nweaknesses. Proper padding schemes, like OAEP, should be used to mitigate these \nrisks.\n\n### Vulnerable example\nIn this example, RSA encryption is performed using an insecure padding scheme \n`NoPadding` within a Java application.\n```java\npublic class SwampSecurity {\n    public byte[] encryptWithFrogPad(byte[] dataToEncrypt) throws Exception {\n        KeyPairGenerator keyGen = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance(\"RSA\");\n        keyGen.initialize(2048);\n        KeyPair keyPair = keyGen.generateKeyPair();\n        PublicKey publicKey = keyPair.getPublic();\n\n        // Vulnerable: Using NoPadding\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(\"RSA/ECB/NoPadding\");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, publicKey);\n        return cipher.doFinal(dataToEncrypt);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this vulnerable example, the `encryptWithFrogPad` method uses the `Cipher.getInstance`\nmethod with `NoPadding`, which is not secure for RSA encryption.\n\n### Remediation\nTo mitigate inadequate RSA padding, ensure the use of a secure padding scheme \nsuch as OAEP (Optimal Asymmetric Encryption Padding).\n```java\npublic class SwampSecurity {\n    public byte[] encryptWithFrogPad(byte[] dataToEncrypt) throws Exception {\n        KeyPairGenerator keyGen = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance(\"RSA\");\n        keyGen.initialize(2048);\n        KeyPair keyPair = keyGen.generateKeyPair();\n        PublicKey publicKey = keyPair.getPublic();\n\n        // Secure: Using OAEPWithSHA-256AndMGF1Padding\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(\"RSA/ECB/OAEPWithSHA-256AndMGF1Padding\");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, publicKey);\n        return cipher.doFinal(dataToEncrypt);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this remediated example, the `encryptWithFrogPad` method uses the `Cipher.getInstance`\nmethod with `OAEPWithSHA-256AndMGF1Padding`, a secure padding scheme that provides\nbetter security for RSA encryption by preventing vulnerabilities associated with \ninadequate padding.\n",
                "text": "### Overview\nInadequate RSA Padding occurs when RSA encryption is used with a padding \nscheme that provides insufficient security. This can lead to vulnerabilities \nsuch as plaintext recovery, chosen-ciphertext attacks, and other cryptographic \nweaknesses. Proper padding schemes, like OAEP, should be used to mitigate these \nrisks.\n\n### Vulnerable example\nIn this example, RSA encryption is performed using an insecure padding scheme \n`NoPadding` within a Java application.\n```java\npublic class SwampSecurity {\n    public byte[] encryptWithFrogPad(byte[] dataToEncrypt) throws Exception {\n        KeyPairGenerator keyGen = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance(\"RSA\");\n        keyGen.initialize(2048);\n        KeyPair keyPair = keyGen.generateKeyPair();\n        PublicKey publicKey = keyPair.getPublic();\n\n        // Vulnerable: Using NoPadding\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(\"RSA/ECB/NoPadding\");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, publicKey);\n        return cipher.doFinal(dataToEncrypt);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this vulnerable example, the `encryptWithFrogPad` method uses the `Cipher.getInstance`\nmethod with `NoPadding`, which is not secure for RSA encryption.\n\n### Remediation\nTo mitigate inadequate RSA padding, ensure the use of a secure padding scheme \nsuch as OAEP (Optimal Asymmetric Encryption Padding).\n```java\npublic class SwampSecurity {\n    public byte[] encryptWithFrogPad(byte[] dataToEncrypt) throws Exception {\n        KeyPairGenerator keyGen = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance(\"RSA\");\n        keyGen.initialize(2048);\n        KeyPair keyPair = keyGen.generateKeyPair();\n        PublicKey publicKey = keyPair.getPublic();\n\n        // Secure: Using OAEPWithSHA-256AndMGF1Padding\n        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(\"RSA/ECB/OAEPWithSHA-256AndMGF1Padding\");\n        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, publicKey);\n        return cipher.doFinal(dataToEncrypt);\n    }\n}\n```\nIn this remediated example, the `encryptWithFrogPad` method uses the `Cipher.getInstance`\nmethod with `OAEPWithSHA-256AndMGF1Padding`, a secure padding scheme that provides\nbetter security for RSA encryption by preventing vulnerabilities associated with \ninadequate padding.\n"
              },
