                "text": "### Overview\nTrust Boundary Violation refers to a cybersecurity scenario where data\nor actions cross between different levels of trust within a system.\nIt occurs when unauthorized access or manipulation breaches the security\nboundary between trusted and untrusted components, potentially leading\nto unauthorized access, data leakage, or compromise of sensitive\ninformation. This breach undermines the integrity and security of the\nsystem by allowing unauthorized elements to interact with trusted\ncomponents, posing significant risks to data and system security.\n\n### Vulnerable example\nIn this example, user input stored in a database is directly used to set a\nsession attribute, violating the trust boundary.\n\n```java\nimport javax.servlet.ServletException;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpServlet;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpSession;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.sql.DriverManager;\nimport java.sql.ResultSet;\nimport java.sql.Statement;\n\npublic class stored_trust_boundary_vuln extends HttpServlet {\n\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String username = \"\";\n        try (Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(\"jdbc:h2:mem:testdb\", \"sa\", \"\");\n             Statement stmt = conn.createStatement()) {\n            ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(\"SELECT username FROM users WHERE id = 1\");\n            if (rs.next()) {\n                username = rs.getString(\"username\");\n            }\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            e.printStackTrace();\n        }\n\n        HttpSession httpSession = request.getSession();\n        // Vulnerable: Storing untrusted data directly in session attribute\n        httpSession.setAttribute(\"user\", username);\n        response.getWriter().println(\"Session attribute set.\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Remediation\nAvoid setting HTTP session attributes based on untrusted data. Instead, validate and\nsanitize the data before storing it in the session.\n\n```java\nimport javax.servlet.ServletException;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpServlet;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;\nimport javax.servlet.http.HttpSession;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.sql.Connection;\nimport java.sql.DriverManager;\nimport java.sql.ResultSet;\nimport java.sql.Statement;\n\npublic class stored_trust_boundary_safe extends HttpServlet {\n\n    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response)\n            throws ServletException, IOException {\n        String username = \"\";\n        try (Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(\"jdbc:h2:mem:testdb\", \"sa\", \"\");\n             Statement stmt = conn.createStatement()) {\n            ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(\"SELECT username FROM users WHERE id = 1\");\n            if (rs.next()) {\n                username = rs.getString(\"username\");\n            }\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            e.printStackTrace();\n        }\n\n        HttpSession httpSession = request.getSession();\n        // Secure: Validate and sanitize data before storing in session\n        if (isValidUsername(username)) {\n            httpSession.setAttribute(\"user\", username);\n            response.getWriter().println(\"Session attribute set.\");\n        } else {\n            response.sendError(HttpServletResponse.SC_FORBIDDEN, \"Invalid username\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    private boolean isValidUsername(String username) {\n        // Example validation logic\n        return username != null && username.matches(\"^[a-zA-Z0-9_]+$\");\n    }\n}\n```\n"
