                "markdown": "### Overview\nRegular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) occurs when regex patterns\nare vulnerable to excessive backtracking. Such patterns can cause long\nprocessing times, leading to performance degradation and potential \nservice denial, even if not directly exposed to user input.\n\n### Vulnerable example\nIn this example, a potentially slow regex pattern is used, which might be\napplied within an internal method, not necessarily taking direct user input.\n```javascript\nfunction isValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    // Potentially slow regex pattern\n    const pattern = /^(a+)+$/;\n    return pattern.test(swampName);\n}\n```\nThe provided pattern `^(a+)+$` can cause excessive backtracking, leading\nto performance issues.\n\n### Remediation\nTo mitigate ReDoS, use regex patterns designed to avoid excessive\nbacktracking and ensure other protective measures.\n```javascript\nfunction isValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    // Simplified and safer regex pattern\n    const pattern = /^(a)+$/;\n    return pattern.test(swampName);\n}\n\n// Optionally, limit the length of input strings, even internally\nfunction safeIsValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    if (swampName.length <= 100) { // Define appropriate length limit\n        return isValidSwampName(swampName);\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n```",
                "text": "### Overview\nRegular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) occurs when regex patterns\nare vulnerable to excessive backtracking. Such patterns can cause long\nprocessing times, leading to performance degradation and potential \nservice denial, even if not directly exposed to user input.\n\n### Vulnerable example\nIn this example, a potentially slow regex pattern is used, which might be\napplied within an internal method, not necessarily taking direct user input.\n```javascript\nfunction isValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    // Potentially slow regex pattern\n    const pattern = /^(a+)+$/;\n    return pattern.test(swampName);\n}\n```\nThe provided pattern `^(a+)+$` can cause excessive backtracking, leading\nto performance issues.\n\n### Remediation\nTo mitigate ReDoS, use regex patterns designed to avoid excessive\nbacktracking and ensure other protective measures.\n```javascript\nfunction isValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    // Simplified and safer regex pattern\n    const pattern = /^(a)+$/;\n    return pattern.test(swampName);\n}\n\n// Optionally, limit the length of input strings, even internally\nfunction safeIsValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    if (swampName.length <= 100) { // Define appropriate length limit\n        return isValidSwampName(swampName);\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n```"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "### Overview\nRegular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) occurs when regex patterns\nare vulnerable to excessive backtracking. Such patterns can cause long\nprocessing times, leading to performance degradation and potential \nservice denial, even if not directly exposed to user input.\n\n### Vulnerable example\nIn this example, a potentially slow regex pattern is used, which might be\napplied within an internal method, not necessarily taking direct user input.\n```javascript\nfunction isValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    // Potentially slow regex pattern\n    const pattern = /^(a+)+$/;\n    return pattern.test(swampName);\n}\n```\nThe provided pattern `^(a+)+$` can cause excessive backtracking, leading\nto performance issues.\n\n### Remediation\nTo mitigate ReDoS, use regex patterns designed to avoid excessive\nbacktracking and ensure other protective measures.\n```javascript\nfunction isValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    // Simplified and safer regex pattern\n    const pattern = /^(a)+$/;\n    return pattern.test(swampName);\n}\n\n// Optionally, limit the length of input strings, even internally\nfunction safeIsValidSwampName(swampName) {\n    if (swampName.length <= 100) { // Define appropriate length limit\n        return isValidSwampName(swampName);\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n```"
              },
              "id": "js-potential-redos",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.9"
              },
              "relationships": [],
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Potential ReDoS - Regular Expression Denial of Service (JFrog SAST 🐸)"
              }
            }
          ],
